    {
      "title": "2. Capstone: Automated Secure Web Tier",
      "content": [
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "One project touching nine of the ten RH294 chapters. Build it as a real project directory, not a single flat file — this is also good practice for how production Ansible projects are actually organized."
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Scenario"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Deploy a small, secured, rolling-updatable web tier across three servers, with a Vault-protected admin password, a reusable role for the web config, and a pre-flight connectivity/privilege check before anything touches real hosts."
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Environment"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Three managed hosts in an inventory group [webtier]"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "sudo/become access on all three"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Project structure to build"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "capstone/"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "├── ansible.cfg"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "├── inventory"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "├── group_vars/"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "│ └── webtier"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "├── roles/"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "│ └── web_secure/"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "│ ├── defaults/main.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "│ ├── tasks/main.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "│ ├── handlers/main.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "│ └── templates/index.html.j2"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "├── vars/"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "│ └── secret.yml (Vault-encrypted)"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "└── site.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Task — build it in this order"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "1. ansible.cfg: project-local, inventory pointed at ./inventory, become=true (Ch2)"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "2. inventory + group_vars/webtier: web_package: httpd (Ch2, Ch4)"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "3. vars/secret.yml: admin_password: <value>, then ansible-vault encrypt it (Ch4)"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "4. roles/web_secure (ansible-galaxy init): defaults/main.yml holds a default index message variable; tasks/main.yml installs {{ web_package }}, deploys templates/index.html.j2, opens firewalld for http (permanent AND immediate), and notifies a handler; handlers/main.yml restarts httpd (Ch6, Ch8, Ch10)"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "5. templates/index.html.j2: uses a Jinja2 for loop over groups['webtier'] to list every web tier host's hostname and IP on the page (Ch6)"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "6. site.yml: a pre_tasks connectivity+privilege check (ping, then ping --become equivalent via a become-required task), then the web_secure role applied with serial: 2 for a rolling rollout, then vars_files loading the Vault secret scoped to a task that just confirms it loaded (Ch5, Ch7, Ch9)"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "7. Run --syntax-check, then --check --diff with the vault password supplied, then the real run, twice (to confirm idempotence)"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Solution — key files"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "# ansible.cfg"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "[defaults]"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "inventory = ./inventory"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "[privilege_escalation]"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "become = true"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "# group_vars/webtier"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "web_package: httpd"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "# roles/web_secure/defaults/main.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "index_message: \"Served by Ansible\""
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "# roles/web_secure/tasks/main.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- name: Install web package"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "yum:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "name: \"{{ web_package }}\""
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "state: present"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- name: Deploy index page"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "template:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "src: index.html.j2"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "dest: /var/www/html/index.html"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "notify: restart web service"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- name: Open firewall for http"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "firewalld:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "service: http"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "permanent: yes"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "immediate: yes"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "state: enabled"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "# roles/web_secure/handlers/main.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- name: restart web service"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "service:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "name: \"{{ web_package }}\""
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "state: restarted"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "# roles/web_secure/templates/index.html.j2"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "<h1>{{ index_message }}</h1>"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "<ul>"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "{% for host in groups['webtier'] %}"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "<li>{{ hostvars[host]['ansible_facts']['hostname'] }} - {{ hostvars[host]['ansible_facts']['default_ipv4']['address'] }}</li>"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "{% endfor %}"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "</ul>"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "# site.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "---"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- name: Capstone web tier"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "hosts: webtier"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "pre_tasks:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- name: Confirm connectivity and privilege escalation"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "command: whoami"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "become: true"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "register: whoami_result"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "changed_when: false"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "roles:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- web_secure"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "serial: 2"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "vars_files:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- vars/secret.yml"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "tasks:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "- name: Confirm admin secret loaded"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "debug:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "msg: \"admin_password is defined: {{ admin_password is defined }}\""
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Verification"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "curl http://<any webtier host> shows all three hostnames/IPs, sourced from facts via the template loop."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "A second full run reports changed=0 across every task — true idempotence, with Vault, roles, templates, and firewall all in play together."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "During the real run, at most 2 of 3 hosts are mid-update at any moment, confirmed by watching the serial batches in the output."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "💡 WHY THIS MATTERS If this capstone works end to end, it's genuine proof — not just a passed quiz — that the RH294 material is usable, not just memorized. This is close to what a real small-team production deployment playbook actually looks like."
        }
      ],
      "words": 536
    },
