    {
      "title": "4. Final Mixed Quiz — All RH294 Chapters",
      "content": [
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q1. What's the ansible.cfg search order, highest to lowest precedence?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: ANSIBLE_CONFIG environment variable → ./ansible.cfg → ~/.ansible.cfg → /etc/ansible/ansible.cfg."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q2. A task reports ok and has a notify: pointing to a handler. Does the handler run?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: No — handlers only fire when the notifying task reports changed."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q3. Can a Jinja2 {% for %} loop be used directly in a playbook's tasks list?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: No — for/if work only inside template files; playbooks use the loop and when task keywords instead."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q4. What's the single underlying difference between import_tasks and include_tasks?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: import_tasks is STATIC (resolved at parse time); include_tasks is DYNAMIC (resolved at run time) — this one fact explains the loop-support, --list-tasks, and --start-at-task differences between them."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q5. In a role, which variable file is meant to be easily overridden — defaults/main.yml or vars/main.yml?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: defaults/main.yml — it's low precedence by design; vars/main.yml is high precedence and meant for the role's internal use."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q6. Does passing --check to ansible-playbook guarantee zero changes to managed hosts?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: No — any task explicitly marked check_mode: no still runs for real regardless of the --check flag."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q7. What two ad hoc commands isolate a connectivity failure from a privilege-escalation failure?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: ansible HOST -m ping (connectivity/auth only), then ansible HOST -m ping --become (adds privilege escalation) — a failure only on the second isolates the problem to sudo/become."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q8. What module parameter trap does firewalld share with RH134's firewall-cmd?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: permanent: yes alone doesn't apply the change to the currently running firewall — immediate: yes is also needed, mirroring --permanent needing --reload."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q9. What's missing if a user task's groups: list silently removed a user's existing group membership?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: append: yes — without it, groups: overwrites supplementary group membership instead of adding to it."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Q10. What's the correct order of execution in a play containing pre_tasks, roles, tasks, and post_tasks?"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Answer: pre_tasks → roles → tasks → post_tasks, with handlers firing after each stage that notified them."
        }
      ],
      "words": 328
    },
